course: dictionary
lesson: 6693
title: Many meanings, one word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around it, because the context tells you which meaning the writer wants. «He is a baker by occupation.» The words «by occupation» tell you that occupation means his job.
explain: The same word can mean something different in another sentence. On a sign, «Maximum occupation 50» tells you how many people may be in a room at one time. Here occupation means how many people are using or filling the space, not a job.
explain: In history, occupation can mean that an army takes control of a country or place and stays there. «Ethiopia kept its independence, apart from an Italian occupation from 1936 to 1941.» The words «apart from» and the dates show that this is about soldiers taking control, not a job or a hobby.
fact: Occupation means a job, or the work a person does.
fact: Occupation can also mean something you spend your time doing, like a hobby.
fact: Occupation can mean an army taking control of a country or place and staying there.
fact: Occupation can mean living in or using a building, like «maximum occupation 50» on a sign.
fact: A good check is to read the sentence with a different meaning in mind and see which one makes the most sense.
exercise: «He is a baker by occupation.» What does occupation mean here? | A sudden fright | A place where people sleep | *A job or the work a person does | A type of bread
exercise: A sign says «Maximum occupation 50». What does the sign tell you? | *How many people may be in the room at one time | How many chairs are in the room | How old the building is | A price for entry
exercise: «Ethiopia kept its independence, apart from an Italian occupation from 1936 to 1941.» What does occupation mean here? | A busy time at the shops | A job on a form | A hobby she loved | *An army took control of the country and stayed there
test: On a form, the box marked «occupation» asks you for what? | *Your job | Your birthday | Your pet's name | Your favourite colour
test: «Mia spends her Saturdays on her occupation, painting.» What does occupation mean? | A room with too many people | *Her hobby, something she spends her time doing | An army taking over a land | Her job at the bank
exam: «The soldiers' occupation of the town lasted for years.» What does occupation mean here? | A kind of tea | A job at the school | A party for the whole town | *An army taking control of the place and staying there
